# Line endings are normalised in the repository and checked out as LF
# everywhere, Windows included.
#
# Git for Windows defaults `core.autocrlf` to true, which would check out
# `scripts/*.sh` with CRLF. Bash then reads the carriage return as part of the
# last token on every line and fails with `$'\r': command not found` - so the
# single gate this project has, `scripts/check.sh`, cannot run on Windows at
# all without this file. It is the first thing any Windows CI needs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so no normalisation is attempted on them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.gguf binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
*.dmg binary
*.AppImage binary
